# bundle_things.voc
#
# WHAT: things tied in a bunch / sheaf (um molho de …) — the cue that "molho" is
#       the BUNDLE reading (open ɔ, /ˈmɔʎu/, written «mólho»), not the culinary
#       sauce (closed o, /ˈmoʎu/).
# WHERE USED: bifonia/scoring.py → score_verb(), pattern «molho de <thing>».
# EFFECT: a match two tokens after "molho" (i.e. "molho de X") boosts the open /
#       bundle reading, overriding the determiner-before sauce signal
#       («um molho de chaves» = a bunch of keys, not a sauce).
# WHY ONLY NON-FOOD ITEMS: edible greens are ambiguous — «molho de salsa» can be a
#       bunch of parsley OR a parsley sauce, and «molho de alho/cebola/ervas» is
#       usually a sauce — so they are deliberately excluded to protect sauce
#       precision. Keep this list to things that are tied together but never a sauce.
# HOW TO EXTEND: add only unambiguous bundled objects (never a sauce ingredient).
#       One term per line, lowercase.
chaves
lenha
flores
rosas
palha
feno
espigas
varas
canas
ramos
paus
trigo
cevada
vime
junco
lenhos
gravetos
